---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quick Start"
  description="Run ClipCut on your own computer in under two minutes with Python 3.10+."
  currentPath="/docs/quickstart"
  section="Quick Start"
>
  <h2>1. Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Python 3.10+</strong></li>
    <li>
      <strong>FFmpeg &amp; FFprobe</strong> — bundled automatically via <code>static-ffmpeg</code>{" "}
      in <code>requirements.txt</code>, or install system-wide with{" "}
      <code>winget install Gyan.FFmpeg</code> / <code>brew install ffmpeg</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Clone &amp; Install</h2>
  <p>
    On Windows, install into a short path such as <code>C:\clipcut</code> to avoid Windows'
    260-character path limit when loading native speech libraries.
  </p>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/Chethankumar443/ClipCut.git C:\clipcut
cd C:\clipcut
pip install -r requirements.txt</code></pre>

  <h2>3. Configure &amp; Run</h2>
  <pre><code>cp .env.example .env
python -m studio.server</code></pre>
  <p>
    Open <code>http://127.0.0.1:8765</code> in your browser. By default (<code>CLIPCUT_ACCOUNTS=0</code>),
    ClipCut opens directly into the dashboard without requiring login. Add your AI key under{" "}
    <strong>Settings → AI</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Pre-download Speech Models &amp; Run Tests</h2>
  <pre><code>python -m studio.fetch_model
python tests/run.py</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
